Donald Trump 's never ending war against what the former Apprentice host loves to term fake news just scored a win against the New York Times in the Florida courts. A win that could come with a $15 billion price tag down the legal line.

Which means, the Gray Lady and Penguin Random House must be feeling, as Grand Theft Auto VI' s Lucia says in the just released blockbuster video game: "Bad luck, I guess."

Gratuitous but satisfying GTA VI reference aside, Tampa-based US District Judge Steven Merryday's order Thursday takes some sharp digs at the NYT, and the publisher over the 2024 book Lucky Loser: How Donald Trump Squandered His Father's Fortune and Created The Illusion of Success and a subsequent piece in the paper. Trump sued all concerned for $15 billion back in September last year, claiming &#x201C;the newspaper&#x2019;s editorial routine is now one of industrial-scale defamation and libel against political opponents" - a.k.a. him. That suit was tossed out, but Trump was allowed to refile and then in July the defendants filed their motion to dismiss. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News CBS And Paramount+ To Air Next Kennedy Center Honors News UK Culture Minister Delivers Emotional Plea To YouTube To "Set An Example" & Remove Russell Brand's Channel

While stripping journalists and Lucky Loser authors Russ Buettner and Susanne Craig from the big bucks action, as well as the NYT' s chief White House correspondent Peter Baker, Judge Merryday pretty brazenly did hold PRH and the paper's feet to the qualified fire over published unsubstantiated statements that Trump committed the series of tax crimes over the years. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

In refusing the Times and the publisher's motion to dismiss the case, the George W. Bush appointed judge wrote: "Anyone who publishes the claim that someone else has committed a crime of the complex nature described in some of the challenged statements and who has not received an explicit opinion from a qualified source after a thorough examination of pertinent facts necessarily proceeds with particularized reason to doubt the truth of their statements and with knowledge of a high degree of probable falsity of the statements; in other words, they know that they don&#x2019;t know, but they are undeterred. Knowing of the necessity for that opinion but failing to procure that opinion is a fine example of the purposeful avoidance of the truth, a knowing failure that remains actionable." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

With the case now set to move towards further discovery and trial, it may or may not be resolved before Trump is supposed to leave the White House in 2029. What is certain is that fresh off his very reality TV stage managed meeting with Russia's Putin and China's Xi, Trump will be crowing about this win for a while.

"President Trump continues holding the Fake News accountable for deceiving the American people, a spokesperson for POTUS' lawyers told Deadline after the order appeared in the court docket.

"Judge Merryday has correctly denied the motion to dismiss filed by The New York Times, Penguin Publishing, and their writers, as to President Trump&#x2019;s powerhouse defamation lawsuit," the flack continued. "These Defendants will now have to answer for intentionally and maliciously defaming President Trump. The New York Times has a long pattern of defaming President Trump in service of its leftist political agenda, and today&#x2019;s momentous ruling is a victory for honesty in America."

On the flip side, having enduring a plethora of Trump attacks and suits over the years, the Gray Lady hasn't given up the fight. &#x201C; The Times is encouraged to see Judge Merryday&#x2019;s dismissal of almost all claims against us,' the NYT's Charlie Stadtlander stated today. "We continue to believe the remaining claim in the filing has no legal merit. We look forward to making this argument as we continue to defend ourselves against this baseless attack on The Times and the rights of the free and independent press in this country.&#x201D;

The second edition of the revamped Doha Film Festival opened with a screening of Sara Ishaq&#x2019;s &#x201C; The Station &#x201D; and a strong message of resilience. For the past few weeks, there was speculation on whether or not the Qatari festival would move ahead given the tense geopolitical situation in the region, which has escalated since the U.S. and Israel began launching attacks against various targets in Iran back in February.

&#x201C;When the odds seemed stacked against us, we could have postponed, scaled back, canceled, but we did not,&#x201D; said festival director Fatma Hassan Alremaihi during the opening ceremony. &#x201C;Perhaps our greatest achievement this year is this very gathering. You are here, and we are here.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories China Box Office: 'Resident Evil' Holds Top Spot for Fourth Straight Frame as 2014's 'John Wick' Debuts in Third

&#x201C;Even in the most difficult of times, the Doha Film Institute has continued to stand alongside filmmakers and support cinema," she added. &#x201C;We have had a difficult year, but we have not ceased to achieve.&#x201D; This year, the DFI has supported over 100 projects and brought more than 60 Arab voices to international festivals, with 55 films in the Doha Film Festival having had support from the lauded institute. Qumra, the DFI&#x2019;s annual talent incubator and industry initiative, moved online in March, but still supported 49 projects from 39 countries.

The revamped Doha Film Festival has transformed the Doha Film Institute&#x2019;s existing Ajyal Film Festival, dedicated to youth and family-friendly cinema, into a more ambitious international event for a broader audience. It has four competition strands: international feature film competition, short film competition, the Ajyal film competition (judged by the festival&#x2019;s youth jury), and the Made in Qatar competition, dedicated to projects made in Qatar regardless of the director&#x2019;s provenance. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The festival&#x2019;s opening film, &#x201C;The Station,&#x201D; centers on Layal, who runs a women-only gas station in Yemen, which is a safe haven during the country&#x2019;s civil war. &#x201C;When Layal&#x2019;s younger brother faces enlistment, she is forced to reconnect with her estranged sister to save him,&#x201D; says the synopsis. This fictional tale based on real events looks at the impact of civil war on the country, just as Yemen is on the edge of a possible return to the conflict that killed 150,000 and brought many others close to famine.

The film, which features mostly non-professional Yemeni actors, is produced by Screen Project (a Ta Films Company) and Georges Films. It is co-produced by One Two Films, KeplerFilm, Barentsfilm, Setara Films and The Imaginarium Films.

&#x201C;To have Yemen showcased at this festival, spotlighting Yemen&#x2019;s culture through music, film, discussions, and to have so many talented Yemenis around us is a real honor,&#x201D; said Ishaq on stage.

The director was visibly moved, stating: &#x201C;It&#x2019;s really important to take a moment to reflect on how it&#x2019;s really difficult to celebrate at this moment,&#x201D; before sending her thoughts to the people of Sudan and Palestine. &#x201C;Watching films can sometimes feel very trivial, she added. &#x201C;If there&#x2019;s something this film taught me, it's that the work that we do isn&#x2019;t trivial. It brings humanity to the headlines.&#x201D;

Ishaq labelled her film as a &#x201C;defiant cry that says &#x2018;we are still here&#x2019; in the face of those who seek to erase [us].&#x201D;

&#x201C;We would like to thank the young men of Jordan and Palestine, who made the film with us,&#x201D; echoed the film&#x2019;s producer and co-writer Nadia Eliewat. &#x201C;Films do not stop wars, do not stop genocide, but it is our means as filmmakers to impose our narrative so the world becomes more open to every cause we show.&#x201D;

The Doha Film Festival runs Nov. 19-27.

Nick Vivarelli contributed to this report.

The American Society of Cinematographers has its 2027 career award recipients.

Newton Thomas Sigel will receive the organization&#x2019;s Lifetime Achievement Award, Robert McLachlan will be honored with the Career Achievement in Television Award, and Dejan Georgevich is set with the President&#x2019;s Award. They will be feted during the 41st annual ASC Awards on March 7 at The Beverly Hilton.

Sigel has established himself as one of the industry&#x2019;s most inventive visual stylists. He photographed Bohemian Rhapsody, which earned him a BAFTA nomination and became one of the highest-grossing music biopics in history. His work on The Usual Suspects for director Bryan Singer marked the first of 10 films they made together, including Superman Returns, Valkyrie and four X-Men titles. Sigel&#x2019;s use of unconventional film stocks and innovative processing techniques on David O. Russell&#x2019;s Three Kings opened new creative pathways in modern cinematography. Sigel's credits also include Drive, Blood and Wine, Fallen, Confessions of a Dangerous Mind, Leatherheads, The Brothers Grimm, Towelhead, Da 5 Bloods and Marshall. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Tom Sigel has consistently elevated the art of cinematography through his bold visual storytelling and deep commitment to collaboration,&#x201D; said ASC President Shelly Johnson. &#x201C;His contributions span an extraordinary range of films and genres, each marked by a clarity of vision and a profound respect for the craft. This Lifetime Achievement Award celebrates not only his remarkable accomplishments but the enduring legacy he has built within the cinematography community.&#x201D;

Also, Julianne Grosso will receive an ASC Award of Distinction, and the Tiffen Company will be recognized with the Curtis Clark Technology Award, spotlighting its creative excellence and cultural influence. Read mini-bios of all the honorees below.

Here are ASC-supplied bios of the other 2027 career honorees: blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Robert McLachlan He has built a wide-ranging career across genres and formats, earning numerous awards and hundreds of credits. He has received three Emmy nominations for his work on Ray Donovan and multiple seasons of Game of Thrones . He has earned five ASC Award nominations for Game of Thrones, High Noon and three for his work on Millennium . McLachlan has collected 16 Canadian Society of Cinematographers nominations, with wins for the theatrical features Impolite and Willard . His diverse television credits include series such as The Commish, Strange Luck, Harper&#x2019;s Island, Human Target, The Secret Circle, Westworld, The Affair, Lovecraft Country, American Gigolo and, most recently, Taylor Sheridan&#x2019;s 1923, Landman and Lioness.

Dejan Georgevich With a career spanning feature films, documentaries, commercials and major television productions, including The Blacklist, Gossip Girl, 3lbs., Cupid, Mercy and The Education of Max Bickford, he has established himself as a versatile and respected visual storyteller. He was recently appointed chair of the School of Visual Arts BFA Film program following a 30-year tenure as a highly regarded professor, where he taught master classes in cinematography and mentored generations of emerging filmmakers. Georgevich served as national vice president of the International Cinematographers Guild, Local 600 IATSE. In recognition of his exemplary commitment to education, the Guild honored him with the 2012 Bud Stone Award for Outstanding Educational Contributions to the art and craft of cinematography.

Julianne Grosso Grosso will receive the ASC Award of Distinction for her pivotal role in co-founding Cine Gear Expo with Karl Kresser and shaping it into a cornerstone event for the cinematography community. Her leadership helped create a space where filmmakers and innovators could connect, collaborate and advance the craft. Cine Gear&#x2019;s influence continues to elevate the tools, techniques and creative dialogue that define modern cinematography.

The Tiffen Company Tiffen will receive the Curtis Clark Technology Award in recognition of its nearly nine decades of innovation and its enduring impact on cinematography. From the Golden Age of Hollywood to today&#x2019;s digital production environments, Tiffen&#x2019;s technologies have helped shape the look and movement of countless films and television productions, providing filmmakers with the tools to bring their creative visions to life. Renowned for its pioneering optical filtration technology, Tiffen&#x2019;s contributions extend beyond the lens to include more than 25 years of advancing Steadicam camera stabilization systems and the continued evolution of Lowel lighting solutions since 2009. Together, these innovations have empowered generations of cinematographers to shape, capture and illuminate their images with greater creative freedom. The company has been recognized with numerous honors from the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences, as well as multiple Emmy Awards for its contributions.

Larry Poindexter , an actor who appeared in more than 175 film and TV shows including &#x201C;The Lincoln Lawyer,&#x201D; &#x201C;S.W.A.T&#x201D; and more, died Wednesday, his rep confirmed. He was 66.

Poindexter had been hospitalized nearly five days prior after he was hit by a car while crossing the street in Studio City on Friday. He died suddenly Wednesday morning ahead of a scheduled surgery to repair his broken ribs. Related Stories China Box Office: 'Resident Evil' Holds Top Spot for Fourth Straight Frame as 2014's 'John Wick' Debuts in Third

Over the course of four decades, Poindexter made appearances on TV shows like &#x201C;The Facts of Life,&#x201D; &#x201C;Growing Pains,&#x201D; &#x201C;The Twilight Zone,&#x201D; &#x201C;Duet,&#x201D; &#x201C;Bones,&#x201D; &#x201C;Quantum Leap,&#x201D; &#x201C;Murphy Brown,&#x201D; &#x201C;Melrose Place,&#x201D; &#x201C;Friends,&#x201D; &#x201C;Sabrina the Teenage Witch,&#x201D; &#x201C;Criminal Minds,&#x201D; &#x201C;Weeds&#x201D; and more. He also had prominent roles on &#x201C;Santa Barbara,&#x201D; &#x201C;General Hospital,&#x201D; &#x201C;The Hard Times of RJ Berger&#x201D; and &#x201C;Days of Our Lives.&#x201D; In recent years, Poindexter appeared on "The Lincoln Lawyer," "9-1-1," "The Rookie," "Station 19," and "NCIS," among other shows. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

On the silver screen, Poindexter is perhaps best known for his role in 2003&#x2019;s &#x201C;S.W.A.T.,&#x201D; though he also appeared in films including &#x201C;17 Again.&#x201D;

Born and raised in Texas, Pointfexter&#x2019;s parents are Tony Award-winning lighting and set designer H.R. Poindexter and opera singer Sue Ann Poindexter. He began acting in college before appearing in summer stock at Dallas Summer Musicals, the St. Louis MUNY, Atlanta's Theatre Under the Stars and The Kenley Players in Ohio. He began his career in Los Angeles as an actor and production co-coordinator with Franklin R. Levy and Catalina Production Group. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In addition to acting, he was also the lead singer and songwriter for the band "The High Lonesome" in the early '90's. He served as an executive producer on Broadway's "The Cher Show" and the upcoming "Saved By The Bell, The Musical."

Poindexter is survived by his wife, casting director Carol Kritzer, and their two sons.

Watermelon Pictures has picked up North American distribution rights to The Accompanist , co-written and directed by actor, writer and comedian Zach Woods, starring Oscar winner Susan Sarandon alongside Aubrey Plaza and Everly Carganilla.

